== pipelined delivery
S: 220 example.test ESMTP sink
C: EHLO client.example.org
S: 250-example.test greets client.example.org | 250-SIZE 600 | 250-PIPELINING | 250 8BITMIME
C: MAIL FROM:<Alice@Example.org>
S: 250 2.1.0 Ok
C: RCPT TO:<bob@example.test>
S: 250 2.1.5 Ok
C: RCPT TO:<carol@example.test>
S: 250 2.1.5 Ok
C: DATA
S: 354 End data with <CR><LF>.<CR><LF>
C: <message, 8 lines>
S: 250 2.0.0 Ok: queued as Q0001
C: MAIL FROM: <alice@example.org>
S: 250 2.1.0 Ok
C: RCPT TO:<dave@example.test>
S: 250 2.1.5 Ok
C: DATA
S: 354 End data with <CR><LF>.<CR><LF>
C: <message, 3 lines>
S: 250 2.0.0 Ok: queued as Q0002
C: QUIT
S: 221 2.0.0 Bye
== errors and limits
S: 220 example.test ESMTP sink
C: MAIL FROM:<x@example.org>
S: 503 5.5.1 Error: send HELO/EHLO first
C: HELO
S: 501 5.5.4 Syntax: EHLO hostname
C: helo old.example.org
S: 250 example.test
C: RCPT TO:<bob@example.test>
S: 503 5.5.1 Error: need MAIL command
C: MAIL FROM:alice@example.org
S: 501 5.5.4 Syntax: MAIL FROM:<address>
C: mail from:<eve@example.org>
S: 250 2.1.0 Ok
C: MAIL FROM:<eve@example.org>
S: 503 5.5.1 Error: nested MAIL command
C: RCPT TO:<root@elsewhere.org>
S: 550 5.1.1 <root@elsewhere.org>: Recipient address rejected: not local
C: DATA
S: 554 5.5.1 Error: no valid recipients
C: RCPT TO:<a@example.test>
S: 250 2.1.5 Ok
C: RCPT TO:<b@example.test>
S: 250 2.1.5 Ok
C: RCPT TO:<c@example.test>
S: 250 2.1.5 Ok
C: RCPT TO:<d@example.test>
S: 452 4.5.3 Error: too many recipients
C: VRFY bob
S: 252 2.0.0 Cannot VRFY user, but will accept message
C: NOOP
S: 250 2.0.0 Ok
C: STARTTLS
S: 500 5.5.2 Error: command not recognized
C: DATA
S: 354 End data with <CR><LF>.<CR><LF>
C: <message, 43 lines>
S: 552 5.3.4 Error: message file too big
C: RSET
S: 250 2.0.0 Ok
C: DATA
S: 503 5.5.1 Error: need RCPT command
C: QUIT
S: 221 2.0.0 Bye
C: NOOP
S: (no reply)
== mime message
S: 220 example.test ESMTP sink
C: EHLO mua.example.org
S: 250-example.test greets mua.example.org | 250-SIZE 600 | 250-PIPELINING | 250 8BITMIME
C: MAIL FROM:<carol@example.test>
S: 250 2.1.0 Ok
C: RCPT TO:<bob@example.test>
S: 250 2.1.5 Ok
C: DATA
S: 354 End data with <CR><LF>.<CR><LF>
C: <message, 17 lines>
S: 250 2.0.0 Ok: queued as Q0003
C: QUIT
S: 221 2.0.0 Bye
stored 3: Q0001 Q0002 Q0003
== maildir
Q0001.eml 295 bytes
    from <alice@example.org> to bob@example.test, carol@example.test
    subject: lunch on friday?
    received: from client.example.org by example.test with ESMTP id Q0001
    3 body lines, last: see you.
Q0002.eml 167 bytes
    from <alice@example.org> to dave@example.test
    subject: second
    received: from client.example.org by example.test with ESMTP id Q0002
    1 body lines, last: one line
Q0003.eml 439 bytes
    from <carol@example.test> to bob@example.test
    subject: report attached
    received: from mua.example.org by example.test with ESMTP id Q0003
    2 parts
    part 1: text/plain, 17 chars: Numbers attached.
    part 2: text/csv, base64, 32 bytes decoded, first line: region,total
